: ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1538, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1538, "cached_input": 79248, "input": 80788, "output": 149}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 114977, "other": 423, "system": 37894, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 78546}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 246237}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "5b76b369-000d-5942-b34e-183bdd194673", "at": 1795734043.8737156, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 38204, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "adbc4dc1ab5ab149462028ffa4a3b51a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "6bc240b9-6305-593b-a153-6d1eb1905b55", "at": 1795734043.8787608, "until": 1795734045.2691777, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 38205, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "adbc4dc1ab5ab149462028ffa4a3b51a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01E8d4FZ35o5Z4ucWq6JVfHP", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -2; git diff c0eaa4d HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-2500", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -2; git diff c0eaa4d HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-2500"]], "output": "```console\n273b82d Brief rev. 10: primary C/T results, k* withdrawn/revised, misfit located in floor, cause unidentified\nc0eaa4d Brief rev. 9: better-inference claim as hypothesis; misfit term labelled residual (estimation + misspecification)\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-## Interim results and decisions (rev. 7; experiment-repo main G/T/S runs, scored on R_m \\ S, not yet on the common target set)\n+## Interim results and decisions (rev. 7; **numbers superseded by the primary common-target-set results below, decisions kept unless the next section changes them**; experiment-repo main G/T/S runs, scored on R_m \\ S, not yet on the common target set)\n+\n+\n+## Primary results on the common target set and what they change (rev. 10; experiment-repo 684d1ac and later, `results/ct_*`, `COLUMNS.md`)\n+Group hold-out, fixed k_max subset, 154 models / 51 groups; 50 shared C/T splits, |T|=109. Excess RMSE over the model's own all-others floor on the same T: **S6+P5 5.0 (k=1), 2.1 (5), 1.3 (20), 0.7 (50), 0.2 (80) raw pts; random-k 6.6 / 3.3 / 1.8 / 0.9 / 0.4.** This replaces the interim R_m \\ S figures as the headline; the R_m \\ S files stay as a labelled secondary, and Deviation 3 records that they were seen first (S2 scored below the floor there because it moves hard cells out of the target; on C/T it does not).\n+1. **Needed k (answer to the task).** k*(excess ≤ 1 pt) = 50 [32, 50]; ≤ 2 pt = 8 [5, 12]; ≤ δ_floor (≈ 1.2 pt) = 32 [20, 50]; the δ_T threshold (≈ 0.1 pt) is not reached on the grid. So the interim \"k ≈ 20 within 1 pt\" is **withdrawn**: on the common target it is ≈ 32–50. The answer is a curve in units of the floor, not a single k; the floor itself (≈ 5 pt on G) is the dominant error at every k ≥ 8.\n+2. **Design vs random-k.** S6 beats S0 with the CI beyond δ_T at every k ≤ 80, but beyond δ_floor only for k ≤ 3 (k=5 undecided, k ≥ 8 \"random matches\"). The paper reports both scales and says which is read where: design helps in a statistical sense throughout, and in a practical sense only for very small k. H2 is supported in that qualified form.\n+3. **The misfit sits in the floor term, not the design term** (floor MSE at k=20 measured / T1-predicted: G 29.7 / 11.8 = 2.5×, S 7.9×, T 9.6×; independent of k). About 55% of the G ratio is across-group extrapolation (random-model hold-out 2.52 → 1.73). The synthetic ladder reproduces the estimation term (~c/M) but **not** a 2.5× misfit, and the real matrix lies outside every single rung (calibration, median calibration, kurtosis = 29). **The cause is not identified**; no combination of rungs has been tested. This is stated as such in the paper: T1 is a design-term result (conservative on the excess at small k), not a floor predictor. Decision 1's wording \"attributes the error\" is narrowed accordingly: it attributes the *design* part correctly; the floor is measured, not predicted.\n+4. **Exploratory training-side k* rule** (post hoc, Deviation 4a): on G, k_hat = k_emp at 7 of 8 ε and within one grid step at all 8; on T (13 models / 4 groups) it over-predicts by 2–6 steps; on S (22 / 11) mixed. Reported as supporting, not confirmatory evidence, with the caveat that G's training and test sides share one population. It is not claimed to hold under shift.\n+5. **Scope sweeps (G folds 0–3):** k*(0.25×floor) = 32 (all training data), 20 (50% of training models), 5 (25%); 8 / 5 / 3 at 70 / 50 / 30% density; 5 on the 75-task suites. With less data the floor rises and the threshold in floor units falls, so **k* in points is not comparable across conditions**; the scope map is stated in floor units with the floor reported alongside.\n+6. **Inference rule.** The selected rank (inner CV) is not the best floor rank under shift (floor RMSE on T 9.56 vs 8.75 at each model's own best rank). That is a hypothesis for part of the residual, not shown to be all of it. \"Better inference would help\" remains a hypothesis until the P2–P6 × S6 table is in (Decision 6 stands).\n+\n+**Main finding as it now reads:** a h\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}